---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const projects = (await getCollection('projects'))
  .filter((project) => project.data.paperTitle)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---

<BaseLayout title="Manuscript index – B-Theory" description="Current manuscript lines, precise contributions, status, and reading-copy access for the B-Theory research map.">
  <header class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Manuscript index</p>
    <h1>Find the work behind the research map.</h1>
    <p>This index describes six current manuscripts and notes. Five PDF reading copies are available below; the Structured Boolean Factorization note is still being integrated. A reading copy is not a journal publication or a claim of external peer review.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="selected-papers-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Selected research</p><h2 id="selected-papers-title">Current manuscript lines</h2></div>
    <div class="paper-access-note"><strong>About these versions:</strong> <span>Reading-copy numbers identify the PDF version selected for this site. Copy 2 corrects author attribution or metadata without changing the mathematics. Each entry also names its source manuscript revision. For questions or an unavailable copy, email <a href="mailto:Brian@B-Theory.com?subject=B-Theory%20manuscript%20request">Brian@B-Theory.com</a>.</span></div>
    <div class="paper-list">
      {projects.map((project) => (
        <article class="paper-list-item" id={project.id}>
          <div><span class="status-label">{project.data.status}</span><h3>{project.data.paperTitle}</h3><p><strong>Contribution:</strong> {project.data.paperContribution}</p><p><strong>Where to look:</strong> {project.data.paperLocation}</p><p><strong>Research status:</strong> {project.data.paperStatus}</p><p><strong>Source revision:</strong> {project.data.paperSourceVersion}</p>{project.data.paperPdf && <p><strong>Site release:</strong> Reading copy {project.data.paperReadingCopy} · <strong>PDF byline:</strong> {project.data.paperByline}</p>}{!project.data.paperPdf && <p><strong>Reading copy:</strong> Pending integration of later results and a named author line.</p>}</div>
          <div class="paper-actions">
            {project.data.paperPdf && <a class="button button-primary" href={project.data.paperPdf}>Read {project.data.title} PDF</a>}
            <a class="text-link" href={`/${project.id}/`}>About {project.data.title} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section-block split-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Research provenance</p><h2>How these pages were prepared</h2></div><div class="article-copy"><p>The research programme and manuscripts are led by Brian Theory (Brian Droncheff). AI tools have assisted with drafting, organization, computation, and review in parts of the work. Each mathematical claim should be read at the scope stated in its manuscript; AI-assisted checks are distinct from external specialist review.</p><p>All current reading copies name Brian Theory as author. Historical references retain the names under which the cited works appeared. The version labels distinguish site reading copies from the internal revisions of each manuscript; they do not imply journal acceptance.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
